---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import BacklogChart from "../components/BacklogChart.astro";
import { homeFigures, humanDuration, fmt, formatDate, formatDateShort } from "../lib/data";

const f = homeFigures();
const asAt = formatDate(f.asAt);
const pct = (f.compliance.rate * 100).toFixed(1);
---

<Base
  title="Reports Parliament is still waiting on"
  description="A running count of the committee reports the Australian Government has not responded to, how long each has waited, and how often the deadline is met."
>
  <section class="wrap hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Senate committee reports · as at {asAt}</p>
    <p class="figure">{fmt(f.outstanding)}</p>
    <h1 class="claim">reports are waiting for a government response.</h1>
    <p class="lede measure">
      The longest has waited <strong>{humanDuration(f.oldest.daysOutstanding)}</strong>{" "}
      — {fmt(f.oldest.daysOutstanding)} days since the {f.oldest.body} committee
      tabled{" "}<em>{f.oldest.title}</em> on {formatDate(f.oldest.owedSince)}. The
      Senate has asked for a response within three months since 1973.
    </p>

    <dl class="stats">
      <div>
        <dt>Waiting over a year</dt>
        <dd class="num">{fmt(f.overOneYear)}</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Waiting over five years</dt>
        <dd class="num">{fmt(f.overFiveYears)}</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Median wait so far</dt>
        <dd class="num">{fmt(f.medianWait)} days</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Met the three-month deadline</dt>
        <dd class="num">{pct}%</dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap">
    <BacklogChart points={f.history} peak={f.peak} />
  </section>

  <section class="wrap two-up">
    <div class="measure">
      <h2>The deadline is not a deadline</h2>
      <p>
        Of the {fmt(f.compliance.assessable)} responses since 2000 where both the report
        and the response are dated in the register, {fmt(f.compliance.onTime)} arrived
        within the required three months. That is {pct} per cent. The median response
        took {fmt(f.compliance.medianDays)} days.
      </p>
      <p>
        A further {fmt(f.compliance.excluded)} responses cannot be assessed, because the
        2000–01 registers do not record when the report was tabled. They are excluded
        rather than counted as failures.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="measure">
      <h2>What this site is</h2>
      <p>
        When a Senate committee reports, the government is expected to say what it will
        do about the recommendations. Often it does not, or does so years later. There
        is no single public record of which reports are still waiting.
      </p>
      <p>
        This is that record. It is rebuilt every week from the Senate’s own registers
        and the Tabled Documents database, and the whole dataset is{" "}
        <a href="https://github.com/toohardbasket-lab/toohardbasket">public</a>.
        Nothing here is an opinion about any recommendation — only whether an answer
        was given, and when.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap longest">
    <h2>Longest outstanding</h2>
    <table class="register">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col" class="num">Waiting</th>
          <th scope="col">Report</th>
          <th scope="col">Committee</th>
          <th scope="col" class="num">Tabled</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {f.ledger.slice(0, 10).map((r) => (
          <tr>
            <td class="num">{fmt(r.daysOutstanding)} days</td>
            <td>{r.title}</td>
            <td class="cmte">{r.body}</td>
            <td class="num">{formatDateShort(r.owedSince)}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="more"><a href="/senate/">All {fmt(f.outstanding)} reports in the Senate register →</a></p>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .hero { padding-bottom: 2.5rem; }
  /* Hero figure: one per view, >=48px, same sans, proportional figures. */
  .figure {
    font-size: clamp(3.5rem, 2rem + 8vw, 6.5rem);
    line-height: 0.95; font-weight: 650; letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    margin: 0.25rem 0 0.5rem;
  }
  .claim {
    font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 1rem + 1vw, 1.6rem); font-weight: 500;
    max-width: 22ch; margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
  }
  .hero .lede em { font-style: normal; color: var(--ink); }

  .stats {
    display: grid; gap: 1px; margin: 2rem 0 0;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(9.5rem, 1fr));
    background: var(--rule); border-block: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .stats > div { background: var(--surface); padding: 0.9rem 1rem 1rem 0; }
  .stats dt {
    font-size: 0.6875rem; letter-spacing: 0.09em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-muted); margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
  }
  .stats dd { margin: 0; font-size: 1.375rem; font-weight: 600; }

  .two-up {
    display: grid; gap: 2rem 3rem; margin-block: 1rem 3rem;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(20rem, 1fr));
  }

  .longest h2 { margin-bottom: 0.9rem; }
  .longest .cmte { color: var(--ink-secondary); font-size: 0.8125rem; }
  .longest td { padding-right: 1rem; }
  .more { font-size: 0.875rem; margin-top: 1rem; }
</style>
